{"parentUuid":"8c179c79-8291-47c2-99ae-132d3798b136","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"ad3b5c11f3a618bca","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J7AnHQBAxKuNNi81xajj7k","type":"tool_result","content":"codex-cli 0.159.3\n2026.10.01-e373342\n2025.10.02-bd871ac\n2026.09.28-64d2043\n2026.10.01-e373342\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# The ONLY writer of cursor-mock/snapshots/ (the snapshots-read-only gate\n# refuses every other write). Everything it writes is sealed; snapshots-current\n# refuses a snapshot whose seal does not match, so a hand edit is caught at the\n# commit even if it slipped past the gate.\n#\n#   capture.sh run <name>    run the scenario in runs/<name>/setup/ against the\n#                            real `cursor-agent`, and add a sample\n#   capture.sh doc <url>     freeze a doc page (e.g. https://cursor.com/docs/hooks):\n#                            its sha256 goes in the MANIFEST; its text only into a cache\n#                            under the git dir, never into the repo\n#   capture.sh drop <run> <ts>  remove one sample (a bad or non-hermetic capture)\n#   capture.sh all           re-capture every run and doc at the installed\n#                            cursor-agent's version, and set MANIFEST.version to it\n#\n# The version is cursor-agent's release date (`2026.09.28`): `--version` also\n# prints a build hash after it (`2026.09.28-64d2043`), which the schema's\n# version pattern does not take, so the hash is dropped.\n#\n# Login: cursor-agent has no environment-only login in this setup, so the fake\n# HOME links to the user's Keychains directory and nothing else (the same as\n# claude-mock's capture). No credential is copied into the fake HOME; the\n# email the login reports is nulled out of every payload before anything is\n# sealed. A CURSOR_API_KEY is never read or passed.\n#\n# A scenario is hand-authored, and only its setup/ is:\n#   runs/<name>/setup/prompt.txt       the prompt\n#   runs/<name>/setup/hooks.json       the project's .cursor/hooks.json\n#   runs/<name>/setup/*.sh             optional: the hook scripts, installed in .cursor/hooks/;\n#                                      hook.sh appends to $HOOK_LOG\n#   runs/<name>/setup/args             optional: extra cursor-agent flags, one per line\n#   runs/<name>/setup/env              optional: KEY=VALUE lines cursor-agent inherits on\n#                                      top of the hermetic env\nset -euo pipefail\nhere=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\nmanifest=\"$here/MANIFEST.yaml\"\ndie() { echo \"capture.sh: $*\" >&2; exit 1; }\nversion() { yq -r '.version' \"$manifest\"; }\ninstalled() { cursor-agent --version | awk '{print $1}' | sed 's/-.*$//'; }\n# The first capture creates the MANIFEST, frozen at the installed version: it is\n# a snapshot file too, so nothing else may write it.\n[ -f \"$manifest\" ] || printf 'version: \"%s\"\\n' \"$(installed)\" >\"$manifest\"\n\n# seal DIR — SEAL lists the sha256 of every other file under DIR.\n# Written to SEAL.tmp and renamed only on success, so a SEAL always means a\n# complete sample (the cleanup trap relies on it).\nseal() { (cd \"$1\" && find . -type f ! -name 'SEAL*' | LC_ALL=C sort | xargs shasum -a 256 >SEAL.tmp && mv SEAL.tmp SEAL); }\n\n# normalize — hook payloads and stream frames into events.jsonl: what a\n# scenario did, without what differs between two captures of the same\nhook.sh\nhooks.json\nprompt.txt\n==> codex-mock/snapshots/runs/shell-exit-status/setup/hook.sh <==\n#!/bin/sh\n# Every event logs its payload.\nIN=$(cat)\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$IN\" >>\"$HOOK_LOG\"\nexit 0\n\n==> codex-mock/snapshots/runs/shell-exit-status/setup/hooks.json <==\n{\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"PostToolUse\": [\n      {\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"\\\"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\\\"/hook.sh\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"Stop\": [\n      {\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"\\\"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\\\"/hook.sh\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n\n==> codex-mock/snapshots/runs/shell-exit-status/setup/prompt.txt <==\nMake every shell command its own separate tool call, never combined with another command or put in a script. Run these shell commands one at a time, in order, whatever happens: 1) grep zzz /dev/null 2) sh -c 'echo SOME-OUTPUT; exit 1' 3) sh -c 'echo MORE-OUTPUT; echo ERR-OUTPUT >&2; exit 2' 4) sh -c 'exit 3' 5) echo FINE. Then reply only DONE.\nversion: 0.159.3\ncommand: codex exec --json --skip-git-repo-check --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox --dangerously-bypass-hook-trust -m gpt-5.6-luna\nhook.sh\nhooks.json\nprompt.txt\n==> cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/shell-exit-status/setup/hook.sh <==\n#!/bin/sh\n# Every event logs its payload.\nIN=$(cat)\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$IN\" >>\"$HOOK_LOG\"\nexit 0\n\n==> cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/shell-exit-status/setup/hooks.json <==\n{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"sessionStart\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"sessionEnd\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"preToolUse\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"postToolUse\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"postToolUseFailure\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"subagentStart\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"subagentStop\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"beforeShellExecution\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"afterShellExecution\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"beforeMCPExecution\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"afterMCPExecution\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"beforeReadFile\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"afterFileEdit\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"beforeSubmitPrompt\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"preCompact\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"stop\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"afterAgentResponse\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"afterAgentThought\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }]\n  }\n}\n\n==> cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/shell-exit-status/setup/prompt.txt <==\nDo these as separate shell tool calls, one command per call, in order, whatever happens: 1) grep zzz /dev/null 2) sh -c 'echo SOME-OUTPUT; exit 1' 3) sh -c 'echo MORE-OUTPUT; echo ERR-OUTPUT >&2; exit 2' 4) echo FINE. Then reply only DONE.\nversion: 2026.09.28\ncommand: cursor-agent -p --force --trust --model auto --output-format stream-json\nversion: \"2026.09.28\"\ndocs:\n  https://cursor.com/docs/hooks:\n    version: 2026.09.28\n    sha256: 7294a2d63b19d79a5283c948afe174cba8b06a7585563d34a2c41b90f5df0d39\n  https://cursor.com/docs/cli/headless:\n    version: 2026.09.28\n    sha256: d767966f4e86012bce9e358c80c8a8e056d4ad0c8e73d74fd036d5acdf32a7af","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8bf1418e-b430-4b8d-842e-9f86e8ecb030","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:15:10.859Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8c179c79-8291-47c2-99ae-132d3798b136","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ad3b5c11f3a618bca","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a26fb63d519ffd330"}
