s refused this work:\n47\t  - Two recorded stream behaviours have no test. (1) Codex: in runs/hook-exit-codes and runs/stops, a command refused by a PreToolUse hook (echo one, echo DENYME, echo EXIT2ME) produces no command_execution item in stream.jsonl, and the extra agent_message items that follow each Stop block (DONE, DONE2, DONE2) are streamed before the single turn.completed. The codex tests only count turn.completed or check the prompt-blocked shape, and none asserts that a refused command is absent from the stream or that the post-block agent_messages are streamed. (2) Cursor: the pretool-refusal stream.jsonl has 'thinking' delta/completed frames, assistant frames and a result whose text concatenates the agent's messages. The replay test compares only tool_call frames, and the thinking frames are neither tested nor listed as a deviation.\n48\tThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/collab_test.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/background_frames.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/run.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/task-stream-frames/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/task-stream-frames/samples/20261003-151527/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/task-stream-frames/samples/20261003-151527/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/task-stream-frames/samples/20261003-151527/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/task-stream-frames/samples/20261003-151527/payloads.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/task-stream-frames/samples/20261003-151527/stderr.txt (and 22 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n49\t  - session-end-hook/codex: the doc (hooks#sessionend) says SessionEnd 'won't run for subagents', and the mock models subagents (codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/collab_test.go), but no test configures a SessionEnd hook alongside a spawned subagent and asserts it fires only once, for the main thread; the other items (reason 'other', last position, no model/permission_mode, output not recorded, failing exit codes advisory) and the cursor subject (reason 'completed', fires last, output not in transcript, declared deviation) are covered. (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n50\t  - cursor: the doc says session creation is not blocked even when a sessionStart hook returns continue:false, but session_start_test.go only covers exit 2, so that variant has no test. codex: the SessionStart matcher applies to source (docs; runs/hook-matchers shows the 'startup' handler fires and the 'resume' handler does not), but TestSessionStartSaysStartupAndCannotStopTheSession uses no matcher, so that is untested. That test also checks only the first SessionStart event, not that it fires once or before UserPromptSubmit. The codex deviation also leaves out the doc's 'clear' source.\n51\tThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/collab_test.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/background_frames.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/run.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/task-stream-frames/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/task-stream-frames/samples/20261003-151527/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/task-stream-frames/samples/20261003-151527/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/task-stream-frames/samples/20261003-151527/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/task-stream-frames/samples/20261003-151527/payloads.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/task-stream-frames/samples/20261003-151527/stderr.txt (and 22 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n52\t  - TestStopBlockContinuesTheTurnWithOneEnd (codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/capabilities_test.go) is too loose: it only replays runs/stops and checks Len(Stop)==3, that the whole rollout contains the substrings BLOCK-JSON-REASON/BLOCK-EXIT2-REASON, and one turn.completed. It never asserts that each reason is handed back as a new user-role prompt (doc: the reason 'acts as a new user prompt'), that the agent produces further agent_message output after each block, that turn.completed follows the last Stop, or that exit-2 with stderr is the block mech