{"parentUuid":"b227d502-4a3f-4a5f-8738-5d07ed2f3237","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ad3b5c11f3a618bca","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffZmvHVQC3wrMw3DFQyk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The shared sub-agent mechanism is not on `origin/main` yet, so I can't route the adapters' sub-agent answer through it and drop `reply`. I checked `git fetch` and `git log origin/main`. There is no `internal/subagents/foreground.go` and no `turnloop.Delegating`.\n\nThe branch is unchanged since my last report: two local commits, nothing pushed, no PR, nothing merged. `sr-checks` still refuses it, for the same reasons as before. The `reply` key is still in both new `background.go` files, and the `run.go` and `turn_host.go` edits are still there too.\n\nWhat I'll do once the foreground-subagent-result agent's PR lands on `origin/main`:\n1. Rebase onto it.\n2. Take each sub-agent's answer from the launching call's `script` field through its `Start`/`Wait`/`Foreground`, and remove `reply` from both adapters and their tests.\n3. Move the dispatch into new files, or a small interface like `turnloop.Delegating`, so I no longer touch `run.go`, `turn_host.go` or `host.go`. That should also clear the refusals that came from touching those files.\n4. Re-run `sr-checks`. If a judge still wants an ADR for scripted sub-agent answers, write the small `adr/scripted-subagents` and cite it from the cells' deviations only if needed.\n5. Push, open the PR, wait for CI, and merge only if every check passes.\n\nI haven't started any of that, since it all depends on the mechanism being on `origin/main`. Tell me when it has landed and I'll continue."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":564,"cache_read_input_tokens":192226,"output_tokens":526,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requ