{"parentUuid":"8e7e158e-98ed-4ed2-940d-cefd7f6f8e93","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ad3b5c11f3a618bca","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffenEaQSWHpS5JATeabb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The rebase is done and `sr-checks` is running again. I'll check the result when it completes, then push, open the PR, wait for CI and merge if every check passes.\n\nI rebased onto `origin/main` (PR #106 and the narrowed-subjects rule are both on it) and dropped most of my own adapter code.\n\n- **Codex:** `main` already has `spawn_agent`, with the `collab_tool_call` spawn and wait items. I deleted my second spawn path. The cell now rests on that existing path, with an `sr:provides task-stream-frames/codex` marker on `CollabCompleted` in `events/collab.go`. The test uses the existing `script` field to drive the sub-agent, and the `reply` key is gone.\n- **Cursor:** `main` already has background shells, the `task_notification` frame and the `task-notifications/cursor` marker. I deleted my adapter and put an `sr:provides task-stream-frames/cursor` marker on `notificationFrame`. The new test checks that the `shellId` matches the notification's `task_id`, and that no other task frame appears.\n- **Cursor limits:** the mock answers a `Task` call as an error and has no `Await` tool, so I declared both as `modeled-surface` deviations in the cell. The recording has the notification after the await, while the mock sends it after the turn ends.\n- **Reply key and ADR:** because the cursor cell no longer depends on a scripted reply, I did not write an `adr/scripted-subagents`. I'll write it only if a judge still asks.\n- **Files touched:** I no longer touch `run.go`, `turn_host.go` or `host.go`.\n\nBoth my tests pass after the rebase. I haven't run the full suites again."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":348,"cache_read_input_to